{"name":"Red Bell Pepper","hex":"#dd3300","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"bell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive instrument made of metal or other hard material, typically but not always in the shape of an inverted cup with a flared rim, which resonates when struck.","An instrument that emits a ringing sound, situated on a bicycle's handlebar and used by the cyclist to warn of their presence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attach a bell to.","To shape so that it flares out like a bell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell"},{"term":"pepper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the family Piperaceae.","A spice prepared from the fermented, dried, unripe berries of this plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add pepper to.","To strike with something made up of small particles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bell pepper","blocks":[{"text":"The bell pepper is the fruit of plants in the Grossum Group of the species Capsicum annuum. Cultivars of the plant produce fruits in different colors, including red, yellow, orange, green, white, and purple. Bell peppers are sometimes grouped with less pungent chili varieties as \"sweet peppers\". While they are botanically fruits—classified as berries—they are commonly used as a vegetable ingredient or side dish. Other varieties of the genus Capsicum are categorized as chili peppers when they are cultivated for their pungency, including some varieties of Capsicum annuum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg/330px-Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_pepper"},{"title":"Bell","blocks":[{"text":"A bell is a directly struck idiophone percussion instrument. Most bells have the shape of a hollow cup that—when struck—vibrates in a single strong strike tone, with its sides forming an efficient resonator. The strike may be made by an internal \"clapper\" or \"uvula\", an external hammer, or—in small bells—by a small loose sphere enclosed within the body of the bell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Parts_of_a_Bell.svg/330px-Parts_of_a_Bell.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/500px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/1280px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/500px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A variety of colored bell peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg/500px-November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg/500px-November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chef chopping bell peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANovember_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_(8223639251).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg/500px-13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg/1280px-13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg/500px-13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"13th c. BC bell, Shang dynasty","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/%E9%8A%85%E9%88%B4_Chinese_Bell.jpg/500px-%E9%8A%85%E9%88%B4_Chinese_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/%E9%8A%85%E9%88%B4_Chinese_Bell.jpg/500px-%E9%8A%85%E9%88%B4_Chinese_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chinese bronze bell, 18th–16th century BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E9%8A%85%E9%88%B4_Chinese_Bell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bianzhong.jpg/500px-Bianzhong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bianzhong.jpg/1280px-Bianzhong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Bianzhong.jpg/500px-Bianzhong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bianzhong of Marquis Yi of Zeng, dated 433 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABianzhong.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Brazen_handbell.jpg/500px-Brazen_handbell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Brazen_handbell.jpg/500px-Brazen_handbell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early medieval folded-iron and brazed handbell from Britain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrazen_handbell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/English_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png/500px-English_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/English_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png/1280px-English_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/English_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png/500px-English_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mechanism of a bell hung for English full-circle ringing. The bell can swing through a full circle in alternate directions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnglish_full_circle_bell_mechanism.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/St_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG/500px-St_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/St_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG/1280px-St_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/St_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG/500px-St_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"English full-circle bells shown in the \"down\" position, in which they are normally left between ringing sessions","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt_bees_bells_in_down_position.JPG"}],"sounds":{"red":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/En-uk-red.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6d/En-uk-red.ogg/En-uk-red.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c9/En-us-red.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c9/En-us-red.ogg/En-